    {
      "sentence_id": 7,
      "text": "The present criminal revision has been filed by the revisionist challenging the order dated 04.06.2024 passed by learned Special Judge (POCSO Act), District Pratapgarh in Complaint Case No. 155 of 2022 in re: Smt Nazma Begam vs Mohd. Haseeb and others under Sections 363/34,\n366/34, 376-D, 420, 467, 468, 471, 167 IPC and Sections 5-G/6, 23 of POCSO Act, Police Station Manhata, District Pratapgarh.\nLearned counsel for revisionist, after arguing for some time, submits that the present revision may be dismissed as not pressed with liberty to file a bail application before the learned trial court which may be decided in view of law laid down by Supreme Court in Satender Kumar Antil versus Central Bureau of Investigation and another Special Leave to Appeal (Cri) No.5191 of 2021, to which learned Shahzad @ Munshaf vs State Of U.P. Thru. Prin. Secy. Deptt. Of ...",
